Core Logic

Pushing: Add every new element directly to s1.

Reversing Order: Transferring elements from s1 to s2 reverses their order. The element at the bottom of s1 (the oldest element) ends up at the top of s2.

Lazy Transfer: Elements stay in s1 until a read or removal operation (peek or pop) occurs.

Transfers only happen when s2 is completely empty to preserve the FIFO order of previously transferred items.
